{"spec_element": "invariant",
 "proof_obligation": "initiation",
 "diagnosis": "The loop invariant '1 <= i <= (a.Length) + 1' has an upper bound that is too loose. Since max_idx < i, when i can be a.Length + 1, max_idx can equal a.Length, which is out of bounds for array a. This makes the invariant 'forall j :: 0 <= j < i ==> a[max_idx] >= a[j]' not well-formed (both a[max_idx] and a[j] can be out of range). It also prevents proving the postcondition 0 <= max_idx < a.Length after the loop, since max_idx < i <= a.Length+1 does not imply max_idx < a.Length. The fix is to tighten the invariant to '0 <= i <= a.Length'."}

